From 6d2102763764747dbf0bb13fab0968724ae33fd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "claudio-michel[bot]" <claudio-michel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 15:00:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(slack): emit normalized gateway_platform_event for
 edits, deletions, reactions

Discord and Telegram already emit normalized gateway_platform_event
envelopes; Slack fired none, so message_changed and message_deleted
subtypes and reactions were invisible to plugins. Adds the missing
fire-sites with the same contract as the existing ones: plain-dict
envelopes only (no raw Bolt objects), dispatch through the
gateway-owned post-auth boundary (set_platform_event_handler ->
_handle_gateway_platform_event, which enforces _is_user_authorized),
has_hook fast-path before any normalization, fail-closed on missing
actor or chat identity, and observer errors never propagate into the
Socket Mode listener.

Edits fire before the already-processed drop so observers see what
routing suppresses; deletions authorize the deleted message's author
(the only identity Slack supplies, mirroring Discord); reactions fire
regardless of the reaction_triggers opt-in, matching Telegram, and
independent of the standalone reaction:* gateway hooks.

Consumer: Tether (Parcha-ai/parcha-skills), a Slack-continuation
plugin that must observe edits and deletions of the messages driving
long-running agent turns.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
